186429952 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\text{ only}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429952 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429952 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f2e036f-6092-5f13-88cc-76a83386c5e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429953 #edb/ref 1080 "images/27/27610876df35c3b1e8e67e8958a5f28e26dfc26262e55994277629789a4bbd84.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429953 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429953 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bd1d4b62-16c5-5abd-aa19-2354fa42b4fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429954 #edb/ref 1080 "images/3a/3aa0329f2b3017616c2010d4674c0dd13d9e277abe790e276a4e294087d6c685.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429954 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429954 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7a42501-e309-59ab-8e88-d5e25b44bfbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429955 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2k \\\\ k\\end{aligned}],\\,k\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429955 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429955 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e832ba8e-38d6-539c-9e5d-09409711b42c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429956 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6d/6d3187a8b906bf3c2a27f2df2d125442ee82a206ae08c33f7442dc7b6b0c88a9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429956 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429956 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f92ae014-605b-50b1-89d8-1b6f8a824d92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429957 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8f32fcaf-528f-5f58-8192-6bdabdbae6cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429958 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f226cae3-dc9e-52a4-84a0-4560715ab839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of linear differential equations above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b59bb2fc-6ce1-5b76-9a55-8b95129f4121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429959 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y=0 \\\\ x-2y=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the first equation is a multiple of the second one:\n\n$$\n3(x-2y)=3x-6y,\n$$\n\nso we can disregard the first equation.\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2y=0\\,⇒\\,x=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2k \\\\ k\\end{aligned}],\\,k\\in R.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429960 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429960 #edb/ref 1069 "q-555982" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429960 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429960 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvector corresponding to the only eigenvalue $\\lambda =0$ of the system's matrix $A$ is $v=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}.$ The vector $w=[1,\\text{ }0]^{T}$ is such that $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$  Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429960 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4195ef0-8343-52e8-8ea2-ad3314d46f09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429960 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =0$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\lambda =0,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, the general solution of the system is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2t+1 \\\\ t\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that ${x}_{E}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are equilibrium solutions of the system since ${x}_{E}^{′}(t)=0.$ These solutions form the line with the equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ in the phase space, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5a/5afce1bca483dbd9bd462810c351d710469b744813cd9f54ea3234f0c7343d35.png)\n\n \n\nNow, we consider some general solutions of the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2t+1 \\\\ t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFor example:\n\n- When ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+3 \\\\ y=t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add it to the phase space:\n\n![](images/40/4019f96cd3c03ec9b0349a0a896951bfa4b0b8f0f828442e002de28d7c8ceb92.png)\n\n- When ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=-1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2t-3 \\\\ y=-t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add it to the phase space:\n\n![](images/df/df4f8378d0c02f982299a349e76c204fd60fb5e014b72e01545cc5dec358aa04.png)\n\n \n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/18/1871e29694b88593a1aeb9ac87536059361f30a2e39966a9ca1180067213d15c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
